{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-27T11:54:26.978Z","data":{"text":"Task complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**`src/cli/inbox-dispatch.ts`**\n- Added `home?: string` to `InboxDispatchOptions`.\n- `inboxDispatchCommand` now resolves `home` (default `os.homedir()`) and a single `stderr`.\n- Card session gets `createWaitRecorder(cwd, 'cards', { home, stderr })` + `home`; `--follow` gets `createWaitRecorder(cwd, 'follow', { home, stderr })` + `home`.\n- Printed output reads via `readDispatch(cwd, config, home)`, `--json` via `readDispatchQueue(cwd, config, home)` — both write nothing.\n\n**`tests/inbox-wait-log.test.ts`** (new) — covers all four scenarios: session log shape, follow log shape, printing writes nothing, and first-seen order.\n\n**`tests/inbox-cards.test.ts` / `tests/inbox-follow.test.ts`** — added a per-test temporary home passed to the session/`--follow` command calls.\n\n**Deviation documented in the result file:** one synchronization line (`settle(() => calls.length >= 1)`) in `tests/inbox-follow.test.ts`. The new recorder wiring awaits a filesystem write before `watchDispatch`, exposing a latent race where the fake watcher wasn't created yet when the test fired the debounce timer.\n\n**Verification**\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/inbox-wait-log.test.ts` — 4/4 pass\n- `pnpm verify` — typechecks, build, full test suite, and lint all pass"}}
